# VERY IMPORTANT — DO NOT MODIFY CODE DURING AUDIT

The first task is ONLY:

```text
DISCOVER
TRACE
COMPARE
IDENTIFY
DOCUMENT
```

Do not refactor.

Do not rewrite.

Do not automatically fix.

Do not delete code.

Do not change database schema.

Do not change API contracts.

Do not change UI.

Wait until the audit report is complete.

---

# AFTER AUDIT

Once the complete audit report is generated, ask:

> "Would you like me to start fixing the issues one-by-one, beginning with the highest-impact root cause?"

If the user says YES:

1. Fix one logical group at a time.
2. Show the files that will change.
3. Explain why each change is required.
4. Preserve existing API contracts unless a contract change is necessary.
5. Do not introduce unnecessary libraries.
6. Do not rewrite working functionality.
7. After each fix, run/build/test the affected flow.
8. Verify frontend ↔ backend compatibility.
9. Verify success and failure paths.
10. Verify redirect behavior.
11. Verify loading/error states.
12. Re-run the audit for the affected area.

